          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vyādha is built on the root √vyadh, \"to pierce, wound\" (MW). MW glosses it \"one who pierces or wounds\", and so a hunter who lives by killing deer (CDIAL 12199)."
